"tf.random.stateless_parameterized_truncated_normal(shape, seed, means=0.0, stddevs=1.0, minvals=-2.0, maxvals=2.0, name=None)
Outputs random values from a truncated normal distribution.

  The generated values follow a normal distribution with specified mean and
  standard deviation, except that values whose magnitude is more than 2 standard
  deviations from the mean are dropped and re-picked.


  Examples:

  Sample from a Truncated normal, with deferring shape parameters that
  broadcast.

  >>> means = 0.
  >>> stddevs = tf.math.exp(tf.random.uniform(shape=[2, 3]))
  >>> minvals = [-1., -2., -1000.]
  >>> maxvals = [[10000.], [1.]]
  >>> y = tf.random.stateless_parameterized_truncated_normal(
